Day 7 — AWS EKS (Kubernetes on AWS) + Containers

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your team wants to migrate microservices to containers on AWS. How will you decide when to use EKS over ECS or Lambda?

2️⃣ EKS worker nodes are running out of capacity and pods remain in Pending state. What will you check first?

3️⃣ You need zero-downtime rolling updates for production workloads. How will you design the deployment strategy?

4️⃣ A service in EKS needs access to DynamoDB and S3 without storing long-lived credentials. How will you configure IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA)?

5️⃣ Pods from different teams must be isolated completely. How will you implement namespace-level RBAC, Network Policies, and security boundaries?

6️⃣ Your application requires autoscaling based on CPU, memory, and custom metrics. How will you use HPA, VPA, and Cluster Autoscaler together?

7️⃣ A workload needs GPU support. How will you configure EKS, node groups, AMIs, and drivers?

8️⃣ EKS control plane charges are high for non-production clusters. How will you optimize cost without reducing stability?

9️⃣ Logging from all microservices is scattered. How will you centralize logs using CloudWatch, OpenSearch, or FluentBit?

🔟 Your app needs an external endpoint with SSL offloading and path-based routing. How will you design this using ALB Ingress Controller?

1️⃣1️⃣ A pod restarted repeatedly with CrashLoopBackOff. What debugging steps will you follow?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need end-to-end service mesh capabilities like mTLS and traffic splitting. How will you integrate AWS App Mesh or Istio?

1️⃣3️⃣ EKS nodes fail health checks due to CNI/IP exhaustion. How will you troubleshoot and fix Pod IP allocation issues?

1️⃣4️⃣ You must run scheduled jobs and cron workflows on EKS. Which Kubernetes components or AWS integrations will you use?

1️⃣5️⃣ A production incident occurred due to misconfigured manifests. How will you implement GitOps for safe, audited deployments?
